Major concerns include:
1. Limited scope of the work: Several reviewers mentioned the limited risk categories covered by the proposed approach and dataset as a main concern. There are also concerns about the limited "unseen task" evaluation and the function-level (as opposed to file- or repository-level) code generation setting;
2. Limited generalizability of the proposed approach: Reviewers are concerned that the proposed agent relies on manual enumeration of policies, bias groups, and CWE types and thus cannot generalize beyond the pre-defined scope (i.e., the seen risk categories);
3. Baselines should be stronger.
